"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1709,"**
Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya, who said: Narrated to us Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi, who said: Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, who said: Mahmud ibn al-Rabi' al-Ansari informed me that he had memorized the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and had memorized a mouthful of water that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had spat from a bucket of water from a well in their house onto his face. Mahmud claimed that he had heard 'Itban ibn Malik al-Ansari—who was one of those who had witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)—say:

""I used to pray for my people, the Banu Salim. A valley would come between me and them when the rains came. He said: It was difficult for me to cross it to their mosque, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said to him: 'Indeed, I have some weakness in my eyesight, and the valley that comes between me and my people flows when the rains come, making it difficult for me to cross. I wish that you would come to me so that you may pray in my house, and I may take it as a place of prayer.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'I will do so.'

The next day, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to me along with Abu Bakr after the day had advanced. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sought permission to enter, and I permitted him. He did not sit until he said: 'Where would you like me to pray for you in your house?' So I pointed to the place where I wished him to pray. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) then stood up and said the takbir, and we formed a row behind him. He then prayed two rak'ahs, after which he said the taslim, and we said the taslim when he said the taslim."""
